Assertions:
[DOM] main menu exposes the catalog entry point ('All products') as a flat mega-menu — there is NO per-item hover flyout in this theme {OBSERVED}
[DOM] every top-level category in the opened 'All products' panel is present as a link with non-empty label text and an href {OBSERVED}
[NAV] category page loads with a URL slug matching the clicked category {OBSERVED}
[DOM] the category page 'h1' heading text equals the label of the clicked category entry {OBSERVED}

Steps:
--- LAYER: Admin (Manual) ---
[MANUAL] Sign in to {{BACK_URL}}/ui as admin
[MANUAL] Navigate to Stores > {{STORE_ID}} > Search configuration > Sorting
[MANUAL] Identify a non-default visible option and note its sort code (e.g. createddate-descending)
[MANUAL] Toggle its visibility to Hidden (HIDDEN badge — grey solid pill appears)
[MANUAL] Save the configuration
[WAIT] Wait 30-60 seconds
--- LAYER: API verification (GraphQL automated) ---
[AUTH role=PUBLIC]
[GQL-OP sortings_after_hide]
  query SortingsAfterHide($storeId: String! $currencyCode: String $cultureName: String) {
    products(storeId: $storeId currencyCode: $currencyCode cultureName: $cultureName first: 1 withFacets: true) {
      sortings { id name isDefault selected }
    }
  }
[GQL-VARS sortings_after_hide] {"storeId": "{{STORE_ID}}", "currencyCode": "{{CURRENCY_CODE}}", "cultureName": "{{CULTURE_NAME}}"}
[GQL-EXEC sortings_after_hide]
[GQL-OP hidden_code_still_resolves]
  query HiddenCodeResolves($storeId: String! $currencyCode: String $cultureName: String) {
    products(storeId: $storeId currencyCode: $currencyCode cultureName: $cultureName first: 3 sort: "createddate-descending" withFacets: true) {
      totalCount
      items { id }
      sortings { id isDefault selected }
    }
  }
[GQL-VARS hidden_code_still_resolves] {"storeId": "{{STORE_ID}}", "currencyCode": "{{CURRENCY_CODE}}", "cultureName": "{{CULTURE_NAME}}"}
[GQL-EXEC hidden_code_still_resolves]

--- LAYER: Admin (Manual) ---
[MANUAL] Sign in to {{BACK_URL}}/ui as admin
[MANUAL] Navigate to Stores > {{STORE_ID}} > Search configuration > Sorting
[MANUAL] Click 'Add' to create a custom sort option
[MANUAL] Enter a unique sort id (e.g. 'agent-test-custom-sort'), a name (e.g. 'Custom Test Sort'), and a sort expression
[MANUAL] Save the configuration
[MANUAL] Verify the new entry shows a CUSTOM badge (grey outline pill)
[MANUAL] Verify the CUSTOM option has a delete/remove button visible in the row
[MANUAL] Verify READ-ONLY built-in options (those locked by the module) have no delete button
